{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba /tmp/cc1-p1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc | sed -n '1,240p;570,970p;1040,1130p;1300,1475p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba /tmp/cc1-p1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc | sed -n '1,240p;570,970p;1040,1130p;1300,1475p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.vm.macro\n     2\t  \"The row-native macro expander (`docs/design/yin.vm.macro.md`, Phase 1).\n     3\t\n     4\t   A process between two media: it observes `program-in` batches\n     5\t   `[:yin.program/batch trees run-index declaration-rows harvest-rows\n     6\t   call-site-claims]` — the trailing element present only when some\n     7\t   member's frontend claimed call-site (C1) coverage, holding one\n     8\t   boolean verdict per member, so every older five-element batch is\n     9\t   still a valid unclaimed batch —\n    10\t   rewrites the selected tree to a fixpoint, and appends one canonical tree\n    11\t   packet `[root rows]` to `program-out`, with one event row per attempt on\n    12\t   an optional log medium. Evaluators know nothing of any of this (decision\n    13\t   1): a macro call is an ordinary `:application` row, macro-ness is an\n    14\t   occurrence declaration beside the tree, and definitions leave as ordinary\n    15\t   syntax or as a literal naming the lowered macro.\n    16\t\n    17\t   Everything here is a value threaded through the step: the macro store,\n    18\t   attempt counter, batch coordinate, and incarnation token live in `ctx`\n    19\t   (§3.1). Expansion failure is data (decision 12); a throw is a defect or a\n    20\t   terminal stream outcome.\"\n    21\t  (:refer-clojure :exclude [flush load])\n    22\t  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n    23\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    24\t            [dao.stream.observer :as observer]\n    25\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n    26\t            [yin.vm.ast-walker :as ast-walker]\n    27\t            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]))\n    28\t\n    29\t\n    30\t;; =============================================================================\n    31\t;; Grammar, rows, and packets (§1)\n    32\t;; =============================================================================\n    33\t\n    34\t(def ^:private standin-tag :yin.macro/defined)\n    35\t\n    36\t\n    37\t(def ^:private working-grammar\n    38\t  \"The canonical §2.3 table plus the one working row the expander interns\n    39\t   and lowers itself: `[S :yin.macro/defined name k]` (§3.2 step 3). It is\n    40\t   admitted only in operand and result packets, never in input or output.\"\n    41\t  (assoc vm/semantic-bytecode-grammar standin-tag [[:name :sym] [:k :int]]))\n    42\t\n    43\t\n    44\t(defn- grammar\n    45\t  [working?]\n    46\t  (if working? working-grammar vm/semantic-bytecode-grammar))\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\t(defn- row-tag\n    50\t  [row]\n    51\t  (nth row 1))\n    52\t\n    53\t\n    54\t(defn- intern-row\n    55\t  \"The full row for `body`: its content address prepended (§1.1).\"\n    56\t  [body]\n    57\t  (into [(jing/segment-key body)] body))\n    58\t\n    59\t\n    60\t(defn- slot-kinds\n    61\t  \"`[[position kind] ...]` for a tag's grammar slots, positions being full-row\n    62\t   positions (address 0, tag 1, first slot 2).\"\n    63\t  [tag]\n    64\t  (map-indexed (fn [i [_ kind]] [(+ i 2) kind]) (get working-grammar tag)))\n    65\t\n    66\t\n    67\t(defn- child-places\n    68\t  \"`[[coordinate child-address] ...]` of one row in grammar order: a `node`\n    69\t   slot's coordinate is its full-row position, a `nodes` child's is\n    70\t   `[position i]` (§2.1).\"\n    71\t  [row]\n    72\t  (mapcat (fn [[pos kind]]\n    73\t            (case kind\n    74\t              :node [[pos (nth row pos)]]\n    75\t              :nodes (map-indexed (fn [i c] [[pos i] c]) (nth row pos))\n    76\t              nil))\n    77\t          (slot-kinds (row-tag row))))\n    78\t\n    79\t\n    80\t(defn- with-child\n    81\t  \"`row`'s body with the child at coordinate `coord` replaced by `address`.\"\n    82\t  [row coord address]\n    83\t  (let [body (subvec row 1)]\n    84\t    (if (vector? coord)\n    85\t      (let [[pos i] coord]\n    86\t        (assoc body (dec pos) (assoc (nth row pos) i address)))\n    87\t      (assoc body (dec coord) address))))\n    88\t\n    89\t\n    90\t(defn- reachable\n    91\t  \"Addresses reachable from `root` through `index`, first-encounter preorder\n    92\t   in grammar order. Assumes the index is closed and acyclic.\"\n    93\t  [index root]\n    94\t  (loop [stack (list root)\n    95\t         seen #{}\n    96\t         order []]\n    97\t    (if-let [a (first stack)]\n    98\t      (if (contains? seen a)\n    99\t        (recur (rest stack) seen order)\n   100\t        (recur (reduce conj (rest stack) (reverse (map second (child-places (get index a)))))\n   101\t               (conj seen a)\n   102\t               (conj order a)))\n   103\t      order)))\n   104\t\n   105\t\n   106\t(defn- packet-of\n   107\t  \"The self-contained tree packet `[root rows]` rooted at `root` (§1.2). Row\n   108\t   order is preorder, which is deterministic but carries no meaning.\"\n   109\t  [index root]\n   110\t  [root (mapv #(get index %) (reachable index root))])\n   111\t\n   112\t\n   113\t(defn tree-packet\n   114\t  \"Convert a projected row set `{:root id :rows {id row}}` (the shape\n   115\t   `yin.vm/ast->semantic-bytecode` returns) to a tree packet `[root rows]`.\"\n   116\t  [{:keys [root rows]}]\n   117\t  (packet-of rows root))\n   118\t\n   119\t\n   120\t(defn packet->row-set\n   121\t  \"Convert a canonical tree packet to `{:root id :rows {id row}}`, the shape\n   122\t   the evaluator loaders take.\"\n   123\t  [[root rows]]\n   124\t  {:root root, :rows (into {} (map (fn [r] [(first r) r])) rows)})\n   125\t\n   126\t\n   127\t(defn ast->packet\n   128\t  \"Project a map AST to its canonical tree packet.\"\n   129\t  [ast]\n   130\t  (tree-packet (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)))\n   131\t\n   132\t\n   133\t(defn- same-value?\n   134\t  \"`=` that also compares metadata at every depth: the transitional address\n   135\t   encoder does not hash scalar metadata, so two bodies may share an address\n   136\t   while differing there, which is an address conflict (§5.3, §7.2).\"\n   137\t  [a b]\n   138\t  (and (= a b)\n   139\t       (= (meta a) (meta b))\n   140\t       (or (nil? (meta a)) (same-value? (meta a) (meta b)))\n   141\t       (cond (map? a) (every? (fn [[k v]]\n   142\t                                (let [[k' v'] (find b k)]\n   143\t                                  (and (same-value? k k') (same-value? v v'))))\n   144\t                              a)\n   145\t             (set? a) (every? (fn [e] (same-value? e (some #(when (= e %) %) b))) a)\n   146\t             (sequential? a) (every? true? (map same-value? a b))\n   147\t             :else true)))\n   148\t\n   149\t\n   150\t;; =============================================================================\n   151\t;; Packet validation (§7.1, §7.2)\n   152\t;; =============================================================================\n   153\t\n   154\t(defn- standin-shaped?\n   155\t  \"A vector that reads as a working stand-in row or body.\"\n   156\t  [x]\n   157\t  (and (vector? x)\n   158\t       (or (= standin-tag (first x))\n   159\t           (and (< 1 (count x)) (= standin-tag (nth x 1))))))\n   160\t\n   161\t\n   162\t(defn- marker-in?\n   163\t  \"True when a stand-in-shaped vector appears anywhere inside a value.\"\n   164\t  [x]\n   165\t  (or (standin-shaped? x)\n   166\t      (and (map? x) (some (fn [[k v]] (or (marker-in? k) (marker-in? v))) x))\n   167\t      (and (coll? x) (not (map? x)) (some marker-in? x))\n   168\t      (and (some? (meta x)) (marker-in? (meta x)))))\n   169\t\n   170\t\n   171\t(defn- slot-shape-ok?\n   172\t  \"Slot kind check. `data`/`key` admit any value here; plain-ness is the\n   173\t   separate `:host-value` rule.\"\n   174\t  [kind v]\n   175\t  (case kind\n   176\t    :node (jing/segment-address? v)\n   177\t    :nodes (and (vector? v) (every? jing/segment-address? v))\n   178\t    (:data :key) true\n   179\t    :sym (symbol? v)\n   180\t    :syms (and (vector? v) (every? symbol? v))\n   181\t    :kw (keyword? v)\n   182\t    :str (string? v)\n   183\t    :int (and (integer? v) (not (neg? v)))\n   184\t    :bool (or (true? v) (false? v))))\n   185\t\n   186\t\n   187\t(defn- value-slots\n   188\t  [row]\n   189\t  (keep (fn [[pos kind]] (when (contains? #{:data :key} kind) (nth row pos)))\n   190\t        (slot-kinds (row-tag row))))\n   191\t\n   192\t\n   193\t(defn- first-defect\n   194\t  \"Run `check` over `addresses` in order; the first non-nil result.\"\n   195\t  [check addresses]\n   196\t  (some check addresses))\n   197\t\n   198\t\n   199\t(defn- cycle-defect\n   200\t  [index addresses]\n   201\t  (letfn [(visit\n   202\t            [a on-path path done]\n   203\t            (cond (contains? on-path a) [{:reason :cyclic, :address a, :path path} done]\n   204\t                  (contains? done a) [nil done]\n   205\t                  :else (let [[err done']\n   206\t                              (reduce (fn [[_ d] [coord c]]\n   207\t                                        (let [[e d'] (visit c (conj on-path a)\n   208\t                                                            (conj path coord) d)]\n   209\t                                          (if e (reduced [e d']) [nil d'])))\n   210\t                                      [nil done]\n   211\t                                      (child-places (get index a)))]\n   212\t                          [err (conj done' a)])))]\n   213\t    (loop [as addresses\n   214\t           done #{}]\n   215\t      (when-let [a (first as)]\n   216\t        (let [[err done'] (visit a #{} [] done)]\n   217\t          (or err (recur (rest as) done')))))))\n   218\t\n   219\t\n   220\t(defn valid-tree?\n   221\t  \"Validate a tree packet `[root rows]` (§1.2, §7.1). Returns nil when the\n   222\t   packet is a closed, self-contained, acyclic tree of well-formed rows whose\n   223\t   addresses match their bodies, else the first error as\n   224\t   `{:kind :malformed-input :reason r :address a ...}`.\n   225\t\n   226\t   Rules run in this order, each over addresses in canonical byte order and\n   227\t   slots in grammar order: packet and row shape (`:packet-shape`,\n   228\t   `:row-shape`), `:unknown-tag`, `:row-shape` (arity and slot kinds),\n   229\t   `:host-value`, `:marker-in-payload`, `:address-mismatch` (after the plain\n   230\t   check, so no host value is ever hashed), `:address-conflict` (one address,\n   231\t   two metadata-distinct bodies), `:dangling-child`, `:cyclic`, and\n   232\t   `:unreachable-row`.\n   233\t\n   234\t   `opts`: `:working?` admits working stand-in rows (operand and result\n   235\t   packets); canonical input and output never do.\"\n   236\t  ([packet] (valid-tree? packet {}))\n   237\t  ([packet {:keys [working?]}]\n   238\t   (let [g (grammar working?)\n   239\t         err (fn [reason & kvs]\n   240\t               (merge {:kind :malformed-input, :reason reason}\n   570\t\n   571\t(defn- packet?\n   572\t  [x]\n   573\t  (and (vector? x) (= 2 (count x)) (jing/segment-address? (first x))\n   574\t       (vector? (second x))))\n   575\t\n   576\t\n   577\t(defn- need-packet\n   578\t  [who x]\n   579\t  (when-not (packet? x)\n   580\t    (throw-prelude (str who \" expects a tree packet\") {:op who}))\n   581\t  x)\n   582\t\n   583\t\n   584\t(defn- merge-packets\n   585\t  \"Union the rows of `packets` into one index, verifying that one address\n   586\t   denotes one body (§5.3).\"\n   587\t  [packets]\n   588\t  (reduce (fn [index row]\n   589\t            (let [prior (get index (first row))]\n   590\t              (cond (nil? prior) (assoc index (first row) row)\n   591\t                    (same-value? prior row) index\n   592\t                    :else (throw-prelude \"Packet address conflict\"\n   593\t                                         {:address (first row)}))))\n   594\t          {}\n   595\t          (mapcat second packets)))\n   596\t\n   597\t\n   598\t(def ^:private pending-expansion-origin\n   599\t  \"The construction origin the prelude attaches to every node the\n   600\t   macro's code builds during one invocation (ruling U1: identity comes\n   601\t   from the construction event, never from comparing content\n   602\t   addresses). `expand-call` substitutes the recorded expansion event's\n   603\t   `[:expansion record-address]` origin for it when the output's\n   604\t   occurrence correspondence is read — the placeholder never reaches a\n   605\t   table, a row, or an event it does not belong to.\"\n   606\t  [:expansion ::pending])\n   607\t\n   608\t\n   609\t(defn- with-origin-of\n   610\t  \"Tag packet `p` with `f`, its construction origin function: `(f rel)`\n   611\t   answers the origin of the occurrence at `rel`, a path relative to\n   612\t   `p`'s root — the pending expansion origin for a node the macro's\n   613\t   code constructed, or, below a child coordinate that retains a\n   614\t   passed-through packet, that packet's own origin function. The\n   615\t   function rides the packet's metadata, so it is content-addressing\n   616\t   invisible and never leaks into a final tree.\"\n   617\t  [p f]\n   618\t  (vary-meta p assoc ::origin-of f))\n   619\t\n   620\t\n   621\t(defn- origin-of-fn\n   622\t  \"The construction origin function packet `p` carries, or nil.\"\n   623\t  [p]\n   624\t  (::origin-of (meta p)))\n   625\t\n   626\t\n   627\t(def ^:private tracking-meta-keys\n   628\t  \"The private provenance entries the expander rides on packet values.\n   629\t   They are host functions, so they must never enter a hashed or\n   630\t   validated data slot (P1-2); every other metadata entry is the\n   631\t   caller's legitimate data and is preserved.\"\n   632\t  #{::origin-of})\n   633\t\n   634\t\n   635\t(defn- strip-tracking\n   636\t  \"Remove only the private tracking entries, recursively, from `x`:\n   637\t   every collection element, map key and value, and every metadata map\n   638\t   (including metadata on metadata) is visited, so a packet nested at\n   639\t   any depth inside a literal payload loses its host-function origin\n   640\t   while legitimate user metadata survives untouched.\"\n   641\t  [x]\n   642\t  (let [x' (cond (record? x) x\n   643\t                 (map? x) (into (empty x)\n   644\t                                (map (fn [[k v]]\n   645\t                                       [(strip-tracking k)\n   646\t                                        (strip-tracking v)]))\n   647\t                                x)\n   648\t                 (set? x) (into (empty x) (map strip-tracking) x)\n   649\t                 (vector? x) (mapv strip-tracking x)\n   650\t                 (sequential? x) (with-meta\n   651\t                                   (apply list (map strip-tracking x))\n   652\t                                   nil)\n   653\t                 :else x)\n   654\t        m (meta x)]\n   655\t    (if m\n   656\t      (let [m' (strip-tracking\n   657\t                 (apply dissoc m tracking-meta-keys))]\n   658\t        (with-meta x' (when-not (and (empty? m') (nil? (meta m'))) m')))\n   659\t      x')))\n   660\t\n   661\t\n   662\t(defn- packet-has-application?\n   663\t  \"True when packet `p` contains an `:application` occurrence, the only\n   664\t   occurrences whose provenance a correspondence ever reads.\"\n   665\t  [p]\n   666\t  (boolean (and (packet? p)\n   667\t                (some #(= :application (row-tag %)) (second p)))))\n   668\t\n   669\t\n   670\t(defn- register-lineage!\n   671\t  \"Record packet `p` in the invocation `lineage` (an atom of entries)\n   672\t   under the identity of its rows vector. Host decomposition\n   673\t   (`first`/`rest`/`get`) hands that very object to reassembly, so the\n   674\t   entry is how a rebuilt packet proves it is this packet retained,\n   675\t   never a content twin built anew. Returns `p`.\"\n   676\t  [lineage p]\n   677\t  (when (and lineage (packet? p) (origin-of-fn p))\n   678\t    (when-not (some #(identical? (second p) (:rows %)) @lineage)\n   679\t      (swap! lineage conj {:root (first p), :rows (second p),\n   680\t                           :fn (origin-of-fn p)})))\n   681\t  p)\n   682\t\n   683\t\n   684\t(defn- lineage-origin-for\n   685\t  \"The retained origin function for candidate packet `c` when its rows\n   686\t   are the very row objects a registered packet carried: the root must\n   687\t   match and every row must be `identical?` to the registered packet's\n   688\t   row in order. Content equality alone never suffices — a freshly\n   689\t   built twin holds equal but distinct row objects and recovers\n   690\t   nothing here (ruling U1).\"\n   691\t  [lineage c]\n   692\t  (when (and lineage (packet? c) (nil? (origin-of-fn c)))\n   693\t    (some (fn [{:keys [root rows fn]}]\n   694\t            (when (and (= root (first c))\n   695\t                       (or (identical? rows (second c))\n   696\t                           (and (= (count rows) (count (second c)))\n   697\t                                (every? true?\n   698\t                                        (map identical? rows\n   699\t                                             (second c))))))\n   700\t              fn))\n   701\t          @lineage)))\n   702\t\n   703\t\n   704\t(def ^:private missing-provenance-origin\n   705\t  \"The origin an unaccounted child answers below its coordinate: no\n   706\t   sanctioned operation threaded provenance to it, so nothing may\n   707\t   relabel its occurrences as this expansion's construction (P1-1).\n   708\t   `output-correspondence` carries the marker through and\n   709\t   `expand-call` refuses the output as `:missing-provenance`; the\n   710\t   marker never reaches a table, a row, or an event.\"\n   711\t  [:expansion ::missing])\n   712\t\n   713\t\n   714\t(defn- constructed-origin-fn\n   715\t  \"The origin function of a packet the prelude constructed: its root\n   716\t   occurrence carries the pending expansion origin; a relative path\n   717\t   below a child coordinate delegates to the packet passed for that\n   718\t   child — a spliced operand retains its own incoming origin, however\n   719\t   the macro's code embedded it. `recover` answers a child packet's\n   720\t   retained origin function when the packet itself carries none (it\n   721\t   was rebuilt by decomposition/reassembly); a child neither source\n   722\t   accounts for answers `missing-provenance-origin` below its\n   723\t   coordinate, which the expander refuses rather than reads as\n   724\t   construction.\"\n   725\t  ([coord-children] (constructed-origin-fn coord-children (fn [_] nil)))\n   726\t  ([coord-children recover]\n   727\t   (fn [rel]\n   728\t     (if (empty? rel)\n   729\t       pending-expansion-origin\n   730\t       (if-some [child (get coord-children (first rel))]\n   731\t         (if-some [f (or (origin-of-fn child) (recover child))]\n   732\t           (f (subvec rel 1))\n   733\t           missing-provenance-origin)\n   734\t         pending-expansion-origin)))))\n   735\t\n   736\t\n   737\t(defn- construct\n   738\t  \"Intern `body` over the rows of its child `packets`; a closed packet.\n   739\t   Every node interned here is CONSTRUCTED by the expansion's code\n   740\t   (ruling U1), so the result packet carries the construction origin\n   741\t   function and the output's per-occurrence origins are read from this\n   742\t   construction history — never inferred by comparing content\n   743\t   addresses: a constructed node whose content equals a retained\n   744\t   node's stays distinct, because its origin answers through this\n   745\t   function and not through its address.\n   746\t\n   747\t   Values entering `:data`/`:key` slots are stripped of private\n   748\t   tracking metadata first (P1-2), before hashing and validation.\n   749\t   Missing child provenance never proves construction (P1-1): the\n   750\t   result's origin function answers the missing marker below an\n   751\t   unaccounted child and the expander refuses such an output.\"\n   752\t  ([body packets] (construct body packets nil))\n   753\t  ([body packets lineage]\n   754\t   (let [recover (fn [child] (lineage-origin-for lineage child))]\n   755\t     (let [tag (first body)\n   756\t           slots (get working-grammar tag)\n   757\t           body (if (and slots (= (count slots) (count (rest body))))\n   758\t                  (into [tag]\n   759\t                        (map (fn [[_ kind] v]\n   760\t                               (if (contains? #{:data :key} kind)\n   761\t                                 (strip-tracking v)\n   762\t                                 v))\n   763\t                             slots\n   764\t                             (rest body)))\n   765\t                  body)\n   766\t           index (merge-packets packets)\n   767\t           [index a] (intern-body index body)\n   768\t           coord-children (into {}\n   769\t                                (map (fn [[place p]] [(first place) p]))\n   770\t                                (map vector (child-places (get index a)) packets))]\n   771\t       (with-origin-of (packet-of index a)\n   772\t         (constructed-origin-fn coord-children recover))))))\n   773\t\n   774\t\n   775\t(defn- root-row\n   776\t  [[root rows]]\n   777\t  (some #(when (= root (first %)) %) rows))\n   778\t\n   779\t\n   780\t(defn- literal-packet\n   781\t  ([v] (literal-packet v nil))\n   782\t  ([v lineage] (construct [:literal (strip-tracking v)] [] lineage)))\n   783\t\n   784\t\n   785\t(defn- application-packet\n   786\t  ([operator operands] (application-packet operator operands nil))\n   787\t  ([operator operands lineage]\n   788\t   (construct [:application (first operator) (mapv first operands) false]\n   789\t              (cons operator operands)\n   790\t              lineage)))\n   791\t\n   792\t\n   793\t(defn- lambda-packet\n   794\t  ([params body] (lambda-packet params body nil))\n   795\t  ([params body lineage]\n   796\t   (when-not (and (sequential? params) (every? symbol? params))\n   797\t     (throw-prelude \"yin/lambda params must be symbols\" {:op 'yin/lambda}))\n   798\t   (construct [:lambda (vec params) (first body)] [body] lineage)))\n   799\t\n   800\t\n   801\t(defn- name-of\n   802\t  [tree]\n   803\t  (let [row (root-row (need-packet 'yin/name-of tree))\n   804\t        v (nth row 2 nil)]\n   805\t    (cond (= :variable (row-tag row)) v\n   806\t          (and (= :literal (row-tag row)) (symbol? v)) v\n   807\t          (and (= :literal (row-tag row)) (string? v)) (symbol v)\n   808\t          :else (throw-prelude \"yin/name-of reads a variable, literal symbol, or literal string\"\n   809\t                               {:op 'yin/name-of}))))\n   810\t\n   811\t\n   812\t(defn- sequence-body\n   813\t  \"The reference `do` lowering: `(do a b c)` is `((fn [_] ((fn [_] c) b)) a)`;\n   814\t   one form is itself and none is the literal nil.\"\n   815\t  ([trees] (sequence-body trees nil))\n   816\t  ([trees lineage]\n   817\t   (let [trees (vec trees)]\n   818\t     (doseq [t trees] (need-packet 'yin/sequence-body t))\n   819\t     (case (count trees)\n   820\t       0 (literal-packet nil lineage)\n   821\t       1 (first trees)\n   822\t       (application-packet\n   823\t         (lambda-packet ['_]\n   824\t                        (sequence-body (subvec trees 1) lineage)\n   825\t                        lineage)\n   826\t         [(first trees)]\n   827\t         lineage)))))\n   828\t\n   829\t\n   830\t(defn- slot-of\n   831\t  ([tree n] (slot-of tree n nil))\n   832\t  ([tree n lineage]\n   833\t   (let [row (root-row (need-packet 'yin/slot tree))\n   834\t        kinds (into {} (slot-kinds (row-tag row)))\n   835\t        index (packet-index tree)\n   836\t        ;; an extracted slot is input syntax READ, not built: the\n   837\t        ;; extracted packet retains the source packet's construction\n   838\t        ;; origin function, descending through the slot's coordinate.\n   839\t        ;; A source no operation accounted for answers the missing\n   840\t        ;; marker, never fabricated construction (P1-1).\n   841\t        ofn (or (origin-of-fn tree)\n   842\t                (lineage-origin-for lineage tree)\n   843\t                (fn [_] missing-provenance-origin))]\n   844\t    (when-not (and (integer? n) (contains? kinds n))\n   845\t      (throw-prelude \"yin/slot position names no grammar slot\"\n   846\t                     {:op 'yin/slot, :position n}))\n   847\t    (case (get kinds n)\n   848\t      :node (with-origin-of (packet-of index (nth row n))\n   849\t              (fn [rel] (ofn (into [n] rel))))\n   850\t      :nodes (map-indexed (fn [i c]\n   851\t                            (with-origin-of (packet-of index c)\n   852\t                              (fn [rel] (ofn (into [[n i]] rel)))))\n   853\t                          (nth row n))\n   854\t      (nth row n)))))\n   855\t\n   856\t\n   857\t(defn prelude\n   858\t  \"The closed body environment (§5.3): the pure standard primitives (no\n   859\t   `require`, no stream or FFI constructor) and the row-native constructors,\n   860\t   each consuming and returning self-contained tree packets. `gensym` is the\n   861\t   invocation-local `yin/gensym-sym`.\n   862\t\n   863\t   The collection primitives are provenance-aware within one invocation\n   864\t   (P1-1): decomposing a packet (`first`/`rest`/`get`) registers its\n   865\t   lineage, and reassembling one (`conj`/`assoc`/`vec`) reattaches the\n   866\t   retained origin function when the rebuilt packet holds the very row\n   867\t   objects it was decomposed from. A packet rebuilt any other way\n   868\t   carries no provenance and is refused downstream rather than\n   869\t   relabelled as construction.\"\n   870\t  ([gensym] (prelude gensym (atom [])))\n   871\t  ([gensym lineage]\n   872\t   (let [recover-packet (fn [result]\n   873\t                          (cond (not (packet? result)) result\n   874\t                                (origin-of-fn result)\n   875\t                                (register-lineage! lineage result)\n   876\t                                :else (if-some [f (lineage-origin-for\n   877\t                                                    lineage result)]\n   878\t                                        (with-origin-of result f)\n   879\t                                        result)))\n   880\t         wrap (fn [sym f]\n   881\t                (let [entry (get vm/primitives sym)]\n   882\t                  (if (and (map? entry)\n   883\t                           (contains? entry :yin.k/function))\n   884\t                    (assoc entry :yin.k/function f)\n   885\t                    f)))\n   886\t         p-first (fn [coll]\n   887\t                   (register-lineage! lineage coll)\n   888\t                   (recover-packet (first coll)))\n   889\t         p-rest (fn [coll]\n   890\t                  (register-lineage! lineage coll)\n   891\t                  (vec (rest coll)))\n   892\t         p-conj (fn [coll & xs]\n   893\t                  (register-lineage! lineage coll)\n   894\t                  (doseq [x xs] (register-lineage! lineage x))\n   895\t                  (recover-packet (apply conj coll xs)))\n   896\t         p-assoc (fn [m & kvs]\n   897\t                   (register-lineage! lineage m)\n   898\t                   (recover-packet (apply assoc m kvs)))\n   899\t         p-get (fn\n   900\t                 ([m k]\n   901\t                  (register-lineage! lineage m)\n   902\t                  (recover-packet (get m k)))\n   903\t                 ([m k not-found]\n   904\t                  (register-lineage! lineage m)\n   905\t                  (recover-packet (get m k not-found))))\n   906\t         p-vec (fn [coll]\n   907\t                 (recover-packet (vec coll)))]\n   908\t     (merge\n   909\t       (dissoc vm/primitives 'require 'try-require 'bytes->str)\n   910\t       {'first (wrap 'first p-first),\n   911\t        'rest (wrap 'rest p-rest),\n   912\t        'conj (wrap 'conj p-conj),\n   913\t        'assoc (wrap 'assoc p-assoc),\n   914\t        'get (wrap 'get p-get),\n   915\t        'vec (wrap 'vec p-vec),\n   916\t        'yin/tag (fn [tree] (row-tag (root-row (need-packet 'yin/tag tree)))),\n   917\t        'yin/slot (fn [tree n] (slot-of tree n lineage)),\n   918\t        'yin/literal (fn [v] (literal-packet v lineage)),\n   919\t        'yin/variable (fn [sym]\n   920\t                        (when-not (symbol? sym)\n   921\t                          (throw-prelude \"yin/variable expects a symbol\" {:op 'yin/variable}))\n   922\t                        (construct [:variable sym] [] lineage)),\n   923\t        'yin/lambda (fn [params body]\n   924\t                      (lambda-packet params (need-packet 'yin/lambda body)\n   925\t                                     lineage)),\n   926\t        'yin/application (fn [operator operands]\n   927\t                           (need-packet 'yin/application operator)\n   928\t                           (doseq [o operands] (need-packet 'yin/application o))\n   929\t                           (application-packet operator (vec operands)\n   930\t                                               lineage)),\n   931\t        'yin/if (fn [t c a]\n   932\t                  (doseq [x [t c a]] (need-packet 'yin/if x))\n   933\t                  (construct [:if (first t) (first c) (first a)] [t c a]\n   934\t                             lineage)),\n   935\t        'yin/sequence-body (fn [trees] (sequence-body trees lineage)),\n   936\t        'yin/make-lambda (fn [params-tree body]\n   937\t                           (let [row (root-row (need-packet 'yin/make-lambda params-tree))]\n   938\t                             (when-not (and (= :literal (row-tag row))\n   939\t                                            (vector? (nth row 2))\n   940\t                                            (every? symbol? (nth row 2)))\n   941\t                               (throw-prelude \"yin/make-lambda reads a literal parameter vector\"\n   942\t                                              {:op 'yin/make-lambda}))\n   943\t                             (lambda-packet (nth row 2)\n   944\t                                            (need-packet 'yin/make-lambda body)\n   945\t                                            lineage))),\n   946\t        'yin/make-def (fn [name-tree value-tree]\n   947\t                        (application-packet\n   948\t                          (construct [:variable 'yin/def] [] lineage)\n   949\t                          [(literal-packet (name-of name-tree) lineage)\n   950\t                           (need-packet 'yin/make-def value-tree)]\n   951\t                          lineage)),\n   952\t        'yin/name-of name-of,\n   953\t        'yin/gensym-sym gensym}))))\n   954\t\n   955\t\n   956\t(def ^:private suspending-tags\n   957\t  #{:vm/park :vm/resume :dao.stream.apply/call})\n   958\t\n   959\t\n   960\t(def ^:private effect-tags\n   961\t  #{:stream/make :stream/put :stream/cursor :stream/next :stream/close})\n   962\t\n   963\t\n   964\t(defn- catch-message\n   965\t  [e]\n   966\t  (or (ex-message e) (str e)))\n   967\t\n   968\t\n   969\t(defn bounded-row-evaluator\n   970\t  \"The default body runner (§5.2): a fresh throwaway ast-walker loaded from\n  1040\t(defn macro-entry\n  1041\t  \"A macro-store value: a self-contained lambda tree `packet` with the AST\n  1042\t   `contract` it was produced under. The store holds only these. The\n  1043\t   transformer runner verifies the contract before it executes the packet\n  1044\t   (Rule R: a persistent or supplied code packet is never relabelled), and\n  1045\t   the expander stamps only what it harvests itself, under\n  1046\t   `vm/ast-contract`.\"\n  1047\t  [packet contract]\n  1048\t  {:yin.macro/tree packet, :yin.macro/contract contract})\n  1049\t\n  1050\t\n  1051\t(defn- verified-tree\n  1052\t  \"The packet of a macro-store value after its contract is verified\n  1053\t   against `vm/ast-contract`: `:contract-missing` for a bare packet or an\n  1054\t   entry without one, `:contract-mismatch` for an old stamp.\"\n  1055\t  [entry]\n  1056\t  (vm/check-contract! vm/ast-contract\n  1057\t                      (when (map? entry) (:yin.macro/contract entry)))\n  1058\t  (:yin.macro/tree entry))\n  1059\t\n  1060\t\n  1061\t(defn- check-store!\n  1062\t  \"A supplied macro store: no reserved name is a macro (Rule R), and every\n  1063\t   entry carries the current AST contract. Returns `store`.\"\n  1064\t  [store]\n  1065\t  (vm/check-bindings! :macro store)\n  1066\t  (doseq [entry (vals store)] (verified-tree entry))\n  1067\t  store)\n  1068\t\n  1069\t\n  1070\t(defn- invoke*\n  1071\t  \"Run one macro body. `entry` is a macro-store value (`macro-entry`),\n  1072\t   verified before anything runs. `counter` is the attempt counter, which\n  1073\t   gensyms read. `{:tree packet}` or `{:error e}`.\"\n  1074\t  [entry operands ctx counter]\n  1075\t  (let [macro-tree (verified-tree entry)\n  1076\t        macro-root (first macro-tree)\n  1077\t        params (nth (root-row macro-tree) 2)\n  1078\t        {:keys [env expected got]} (bind-arguments params operands)]\n  1079\t    (if-not env\n  1080\t      {:error {:kind :arity, :macro macro-root, :expected expected, :got got}}\n  1081\t      (let [n (volatile! 0)\n  1082\t            token (get-in ctx [:incarnation :yin.expander/token])\n  1083\t            gensym (fn [prefix]\n  1084\t                     (let [i @n]\n  1085\t                       (vswap! n inc)\n  1086\t                       (symbol (str (if (symbol? prefix) (name prefix) prefix)\n  1087\t                                    \"__\" token \"_\" counter \"_\" i))))\n  1088\t            lineage (atom [])\n  1089\t            _ (doseq [p operands] (register-lineage! lineage p))\n  1090\t            run (or (:eval ctx) bounded-row-evaluator)\n  1091\t            {:keys [value error]} (run {:macro-tree macro-tree,\n  1092\t                                        :contract (:yin.macro/contract entry),\n  1093\t                                        :env env,\n  1094\t                                        :prelude (prelude gensym lineage),\n  1095\t                                        :max-steps (get-in ctx [:guards :max-steps])})]\n  1096\t        (if error\n  1097\t          {:error (assoc error :macro macro-root)}\n  1098\t          {:tree (if (and (packet? value)\n  1099\t                          (nil? (origin-of-fn value)))\n  1100\t                   (if-some [f (lineage-origin-for lineage value)]\n  1101\t                     (with-origin-of value f)\n  1102\t                     value)\n  1103\t                   value)})))))\n  1104\t\n  1105\t\n  1106\t(def default-guards\n  1107\t  {:max-depth 100,\n  1108\t   :max-rows-per-expansion 10000,\n  1109\t   :max-rows-per-batch nil,\n  1110\t   :max-steps 100000})\n  1111\t\n  1112\t\n  1113\t(defn invoke\n  1114\t  \"Run `entry`, a macro-store value (`macro-entry`: a self-contained lambda\n  1115\t   packet and its AST contract), on `operand-trees` and return its result\n  1116\t   tree packet, unvalidated. The contract is verified first\n  1117\t   (`:contract-missing`, `:contract-mismatch`, thrown). Gensyms use\n  1118\t   `(:attempt ctx)` as the attempt counter. Throws `ex-info` carrying the\n  1119\t   error data on an arity, guard, suspension, or body failure.\"\n  1120\t  [entry operand-trees ctx]\n  1121\t  (let [ctx (update ctx :guards #(merge default-guards %))\n  1122\t        {:keys [tree error]} (invoke* entry (vec operand-trees) ctx\n  1123\t                                      (:attempt ctx))]\n  1124\t    (when error\n  1125\t      (throw (ex-info \"Macro invocation failed\" error)))\n  1126\t    tree))\n  1127\t\n  1128\t\n  1129\t;; =============================================================================\n  1130\t;; Tail marking and lowering (§6, §3.2 steps 6-7)\n  1300\t   a store entry that no enclosing lambda parameter shadows.\"\n  1301\t  [st operator shadow]\n  1302\t  (let [row (get (:index st) operator)]\n  1303\t    (when (and (= :variable (row-tag row))\n  1304\t               (not (contains? shadow (nth row 2))))\n  1305\t      (get (:store st) (nth row 2)))))\n  1306\t\n  1307\t\n  1308\t(defn- record-event\n  1309\t  [st event-row*]\n  1310\t  (update st :events conj event-row*))\n  1311\t\n  1312\t\n  1313\t(defn- guard-batch-rows\n  1314\t  [st]\n  1315\t  (let [limit (get-in st [:ctx :guards :max-rows-per-batch])\n  1316\t        n (count (:index st))]\n  1317\t    (when (and limit (> n limit))\n  1318\t      {:kind :row-guard, :scope :batch, :rows n})))\n  1319\t\n  1320\t\n  1321\t(defn- merge-output\n  1322\t  \"Merge a validated result packet into the working index; an address whose\n  1323\t   working body differs is an `:address-conflict`.\"\n  1324\t  [st [_ rows]]\n  1325\t  (reduce (fn [st row]\n  1326\t            (let [prior (get (:index st) (first row))]\n  1327\t              (cond (nil? prior) (assoc-in st [:index (first row)] row)\n  1328\t                    (same-value? prior row) st\n  1329\t                    :else (reduced (assoc st ::conflict (first row))))))\n  1330\t          st\n  1331\t          rows))\n  1332\t\n  1333\t\n  1334\t(declare expand-node)\n  1335\t\n  1336\t\n  1337\t(defn- output-correspondence\n  1338\t  \"The per-occurrence correspondence of the expansion's output (ruling\n  1339\t   U1): for every `:application` occurrence of output packet `tree`, at\n  1340\t   its path relative to the output root, `:constructed` when the\n  1341\t   expansion's code built that node, or `[:retained origin]` when the\n  1342\t   node is input syntax retained with its own incoming origin. The\n  1343\t   classification is the construction origin function the prelude\n  1344\t   threaded through the packets the macro's code built — never a\n  1345\t   comparison of content addresses; the recorded expansion event\n  1346\t   retains the answer, and the site table derives each marked\n  1347\t   occurrence's origin from it. An occurrence no operation accounted\n  1348\t   for reads `::missing-provenance`; `expand-call` refuses such an\n  1349\t   output, so the marker is retained in no event.\"\n  1350\t  [tree ofn]\n  1351\t  (into {}\n  1352\t        (map (fn [path]\n  1353\t               (let [o (ofn path)]\n  1354\t                 [path (cond (= pending-expansion-origin o) :constructed\n  1355\t                             (= missing-provenance-origin o)\n  1356\t                             ::missing-provenance\n  1357\t                             :else [:retained o])])))\n  1358\t        (sort-by pr-str\n  1359\t                 (map second\n  1360\t                      (vm/application-occurrences (packet->row-set tree))))))\n  1361\t\n  1362\t\n  1363\t(defn- expand-call\n  1364\t  \"One recognized call: allocate an attempt, begin its event before any\n  1365\t   guard or invocation, run the transformer on the operand packets, validate\n  1366\t   and merge the result, finish the event, and reconsider the result at the\n  1367\t   same occurrence with depth + 1.\n  1368\t\n  1369\t   Each operand packet enters the invocation carrying its occurrence\n  1370\t   origin function — the enclosing walk's origin at the operand's own\n  1371\t   absolute path — and the prelude threads it through every node the\n  1372\t   macro's code constructs (ruling U1): a spliced operand retains its\n  1373\t   own incoming origin, a built node carries the pending expansion\n  1374\t   origin. The output's per-occurrence correspondence is read from that\n  1375\t   construction history, retained in the event record, and the\n  1376\t   recursive walk answers origins from the record — never from\n  1377\t   comparing content addresses.\"\n  1378\t  [st address entry {:keys [path rel frame shadow depth origin-of]}]\n  1379\t  (let [[st counter] (allocate-attempt st)\n  1380\t        ctx (:ctx st)\n  1381\t        macro-root (first (:yin.macro/tree entry))\n  1382\t        begin (fn [output error correspondence]\n  1383\t                (event-row (attempt-id ctx counter)\n  1384\t                           (:source-batch st)\n  1385\t                           (when-not (:parent frame)\n  1386\t                             (source-origin ctx (:source-batch st) (:tree-index frame)))\n  1387\t                           (:parent frame)\n  1388\t                           (:root frame)\n  1389\t                           rel\n  1390\t                           macro-root\n  1391\t                           output\n  1392\t                           error\n  1393\t                           correspondence))\n  1394\t        failed (fn [st error]\n  1395\t                 (-> st (record-event (begin nil error nil)) (fail error)))\n  1396\t        guards (:guards ctx)]\n  1397\t    (if (>= depth (:max-depth guards))\n  1398\t      [(failed st {:kind :depth-guard, :depth depth, :path path}) address]\n  1399\t      (let [row (get (:index st) address)\n  1400\t            operands (map-indexed\n  1401\t                      (fn [i a]\n  1402\t                        (with-origin-of (packet-of (:index st) a)\n  1403\t                          (fn [rel]\n  1404\t                            (origin-of (into (conj path [3 i]) rel)))))\n  1405\t                      (nth row 3))\n  1406\t            {:keys [tree error]} (invoke* entry operands ctx counter)\n  1407\t            invalid (fn [reason]\n  1408\t                      {:kind :invalid-output, :macro macro-root, :path path,\n  1409\t                       :reason reason})]\n  1410\t        (if error\n  1411\t          [(failed st error) address]\n  1412\t          (if-let [e (valid-tree? tree {:working? true})]\n  1413\t            [(failed st (invalid (:reason e))) address]\n  1414\t            (let [n (count (set (map first (second tree))))]\n  1415\t              (if (> n (:max-rows-per-expansion guards))\n  1416\t                [(failed st {:kind :row-guard, :scope :expansion, :rows n}) address]\n  1417\t                (let [st' (merge-output st tree)]\n  1418\t                  (if (::conflict st')\n  1419\t                    [(failed st (invalid :address-conflict)) address]\n  1420\t                    (if-let [e (guard-batch-rows st')]\n  1421\t                      [(failed st' e) address]\n  1422\t                      (if (and (nil? (origin-of-fn tree))\n  1423\t                               (packet-has-application? tree))\n  1424\t                        ;; missing provenance never proves construction\n  1425\t                        ;; (P1-1): an application-bearing output no\n  1426\t                        ;; sanctioned operation accounted for is refused,\n  1427\t                        ;; never relabelled with this expansion's origin\n  1428\t                        [(failed st' (invalid :missing-provenance)) address]\n  1429\t                        (let [;; the output's construction origin function\n  1430\t                            ;; (ruling U1), threaded by the prelude through\n  1431\t                            ;; every packet it built or reassembled; the\n  1432\t                            ;; fallback is reached only by an output\n  1433\t                            ;; without applications, whose correspondence\n  1434\t                            ;; never consults it\n  1435\t                            ofn (or (origin-of-fn tree)\n  1436\t                                    (fn [_] pending-expansion-origin))\n  1437\t                            corr (output-correspondence tree ofn)]\n  1438\t                        (if (some #(= ::missing-provenance %) (vals corr))\n  1439\t                          [(failed st' (invalid :missing-provenance)) address]\n  1440\t                          (let [out (first tree)\n  1441\t                            ev (begin out nil corr)\n  1442\t                            st' (-> st'\n  1443\t                                    (record-event ev)\n  1444\t                                    (update :produced\n  1445\t                                            (fn [p]\n  1446\t                                              (if (some #(= out (first %)) p)\n  1447\t                                                p\n  1448\t                                                (conj p (packet-of (:index st') out))))))]\n  1449\t                        (expand-node st' out\n  1450\t                                     {:path path,\n  1451\t                                      :rel [],\n  1452\t                                      :frame {:parent (first ev), :root out},\n  1453\t                                      :shadow shadow,\n  1454\t                                      :depth (inc depth),\n  1455\t                                      ;; per-occurrence origins read from\n  1456\t                                      ;; the RETAINED correspondence (§2.1,\n  1457\t                                      ;; §8): a `[:retained origin]` names\n  1458\t                                      ;; the incoming origin the syntax\n  1459\t                                      ;; already carried, a `:constructed`\n  1460\t                                      ;; occurrence names the recorded\n  1461\t                                      ;; expansion event — the record the\n  1462\t                                      ;; correspondence is retained in\n  1463\t                                      :origin-of\n  1464\t                                      (fn [abs-path]\n  1465\t                                        (let [o (get corr (subvec abs-path (count path)))]\n  1466\t                                          (if (and (vector? o) (= :retained (first o)))\n  1467\t                                            (second o)\n  1468\t                                            [:expansion (first ev)])))}))))))))))))))))\n  1469\t\n  1470\t\n  1471\t(defn- expand-children\n  1472\t  \"Expand `row`'s children in order `places` under per-child shadows;\n  1473\t   `[st address']`, rebuilding the row when any child changed.\"\n  1474\t  [st row places shadow-of {:keys [path rel] :as loc}]\n  1475\t  (let [[st children']\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
