aster @ f707e0aba (pushed); h30 @ 6188b98a6 (codex round 5 live)\\\\n178:Done: (1) Muse rounds 3+4 both died on 429 subscription exhaustion (daily window resets 2026-11-03 13:41 UTC); muse's auth store holds ONLY the OAuth subscription — no API key was ever stored, so the overflow lane needs an owner-supplied key; round 3's slice9_declarations.edn preserved. (2) Owner supplied a mistral API key mid-turn; stored at ~/.config/mistral/env (chmod 600, OUTSIDE the repo — the secret appears in no committed file, log, or routing entry) and sourced per run. Measured: vibe's bare `mistral-large` alias is dead (the reference list is stale — the API wants dated IDs); vibe's own alias `mistral-4.0` works (probe OK). The working implementation invocation: `set -a; . ~/.config/mistral/env; set +a; vibe --model mistral-4.0 --agent accept-edits`. (3) Codex round 5 (post-reset) is running H3-0 in the h30 worktree — live edits to latte_oracle_test.clj within 90 seconds of dispatch; mistral takes the next implementation slot per the owner's directive.\\\\n180:Verification: vibe probe OK on mistral-4.0; codex round 5 journal active.\\\\n181:Delegates: codex (H3-0 round 5, IN FLIGHT); mistral-4.0 (READY, next implementation round); muse (exhausted until tomorrow); kimi (queued for reviews).\\\\n182:Next: codex round 5 returns -> full oracle verification by the seat -> kimi code-quality review (the muse/mistral gate applied to the review where useful) -> compiler + disposition-guard reviews -> land -> H3-1 to mistral.\\\\n189:Done: (1) Owner: \\\\\\\"don't use codex until farther notice. use vibe for implementation and kimi for review\\\\\\\" — the running codex H3-0 round 5 was killed (it had live partial edits to the evidence/gate records and a findings file; the tracked partials were reset, its findings file kept untracked for my diagnostics only, NOT fed to the vibe round — unreviewed claims stay out of the next implementer's inputs). (2) Two dispatch corrections on the way to a live