pretended). (3) The checklist is now a binding Redo-requirements section in the brief, and vibe round 2 (redo) is dispatched and live.\\\\n201:Decisions: the owner's trust gate worked as designed — the muse/mistral pipeline caught the failure before anything landed, twice over (my verification for structure, kimi for design honesty). No rejected partial is reused as input to the redo except the declarations file kimi explicitly retained.\\\\n211:Done: (1) With no answer to the lane question, the seat implemented H3-0 directly per the recommendation. Reading the pristine harness revealed the truth the delegates had missed: the ENTIRE H3-0 machinery already exists at HEAD — the classifier `kernel-host-value-deviation` with exact guards and negative-control tests (including the forged-descriptor rejection), `kernel-row` recording `:recorded-deviation` statuses, and the writer emitting `:recorded-portability-boundaries` from classified rows. The SINGLE root cause of the whole regression is astra's r1 finding: the classifier's `(values/closure? meta)` is representation-stale — the reconciled compiler's guest closure at :meta is the admitted §8.10 descriptor map (measured: clojure.lang.PersistentArrayMap with :clj/type :function, :yang.call/entry, :clj/admission), so the check fails, deviations come back empty, the writer honestly records none, and the 2285 assertion fails. The vibe rounds \\\\\\\"fixed\\\\\\\" everything EXCEPT this (round 2 even replaced the working check with an invented shape). (2) The seat's implementation: `kernel-callable-descriptor?` validating the genuine descriptor (function type marker + closure entry + closure admission witness — codebase-true shapes, not invented ones); the classifier accepts either representation; the versioned declarations file drives boundary/upstream-value/reason with revalidation guards (declared message == live message, declared script == live script, normalized); negative controls extended (both representations classify; forgeries — missing admission, non-closure entry, wrong type marker, invented shape — refuse; a mutated declaration fails via with-redefs); the writer gained a `dir` overload so the round-trip test exercises the REAL writer against a temp directory replaying the checked-in evidence (no fixture recompute). The muse round's declarations file was retained as-is (kimi had retained it).\\\\n233:Done: (1) Owner: \\\\\\\"reroute all implementation to agy\\\\\\\". Probed the installed agy 1.4.12: the reference's model aliases are stale (gemini-3.1-pro-high rejected; live list = Gemini 4 Argon (High/Medium/Low), Gemini 3.8 Flash, Claude Opus 5.5, Claude Sonnet 5.5, GPT-OSS 120B); --effort is unsupported for Gemini 4 Argon (effort is part of the display name). The decisive probe: `agy --model \\\\\\\"Gemini 4 Argon (High)\\\\\\\" --mode accept-edits --sandbox -p …` RUNS SHELL headless and reports truthfully (the command executed, the result file written) — the first implementation lane that can run tests itself, unlike muse (approval stall) and vibe (shell denial + a fabricated success reply). Recorded in routing-status with the stale-alias note. (2) H3-1 (the blocked-fixture diagnosis, per the approved plan) dispatched to agy in the h31 worktree: the four-cell packet (fixture x C-evaluator) with pinned identities/actual steps/terminal reasons, the phase-boundary and step-counter-reset check, bounded exhaustion snapshots, instrumented-vs-uninstrumented including check-accepted's completing semantic run, a minimal reproduction if repetition appears; budget trials 2M/4M/8M authorized as diagnostics only; no shared-runtime changes without a ruling; diagnostics carry zero coverage. The brief is in the worktree (BRIEF-h3-1.md) and collab/.\\\\n475:Done: (1) The H3-3 prep round delivered 413e991d: the family design covering all 20 enumerated arities + a 43-prediction A-verify script. SEAT-RUN INDEPENDENTLY: H3-3-A-VERIFY: PASS (43/43) against pinned upstream 86fca0d1 (entry: -ma