pr-str scope ids (full identity kept), the one-origin-per-occurrence rule now enforced in EVERY validator mode with the same diagnostic, two regression tests added (17/200/0; kondo 0/0); pushed. (5) The exception-track r0 kit landed on master (0fa3ff7a, steward note 1795200000000) — R3 dispatch precondition met, still sequenced behind cc1 landing.\\\\nDecision pending THE OWNER: the occurrence-identity ruling — per-occurrence provenance for identical subtrees requires either (a) composition-supplied durable admission identities (the composition asserts which admissions are distinct events), or (b) admission-minted occurrence identity (admission-time token distinguishes otherwise-identical occurrences). In a content-addressed store identical content IS one address (unitarity) — whether \\\\\\\"two occurrences of identical content\\\\\\\" is meaningful, and who decides distinctness, is the owner's call. My recommendation: (a) — it keeps the unitarity axiom (identity never minted from structure) and puts distinctness where the knowledge is (the composition).\\\\nDelegates: oracle full run (background); shiva remote battery at d91489f7 (background).\\\\nNext: both green + the owner's allocator ruling → the design-level fix → astra re-check → codex gate → land → R3 dispatch → adoption rounds 2-4 + D1.\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n19:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_8\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc '/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git log -12 --oneline fa70516f; /Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git show --stat 847aa885; /Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git diff --stat 368297c3...fa70516f'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"fa70516f Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/master' into cc1-rebased\\\\n368297c3 docs(yang-clojure): the occurrence-identity ruling is SIGNED OFF — ruling of record; the codex cc1 reject is answered\