ence of the stand-in-lowered, tail-marked tree\\\\n  1369\\\\t   that actually executes. The frontend's own markers named the\\\\n  1370\\\\t   pre-expansion tree; expansion, tail marking and stand-in lowering\\\\n  1371\\\\t   recompute roots and paths, so no pre-expansion table can cover this\\\\n  1372\\\\t   tree and the table is finalized here, over the finished rows.\\\\n  1373\\\\t\\\\n  1374\\\\t   Each row's origin is that occurrence's REAL origin (design §2.1,\\\\n  1375\\\\t   §2.3): `occurrence-origins` maps the final occurrence path to the\\\\n  1376\\\\t   origin of the admission or generation event that produced the\\\\n  1377\\\\t   application syntax at that path — the admitted run member's source\\\\n  1378\\\\t   origin for retained syntax (a no-op expansion keeps it valid), and\\\\n  1379\\\\t   the `[:expansion record-address]` of the recorded expansion event\\\\n  1380\\\\t   whose output introduced generated syntax. No expansion-record\\\\n  1381\\\\t   address is fabricated: only event rows the expander actually\\\\n  1382\\\\t   recorded appear. The table is therefore the explicit\\\\n  1383\\\\t   final-root correspondence §2.3 requires — every generated occurrence\\\\n  1384\\\\t   names its producing record, so an attribution consumer can reach the\\\\n  1385\\\\t   event (its input root, call path, macro root, output root) from the\\\\n  1386\\\\t   row alone.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  1387\\\\t  [row-set occurrence-origins admission-origin]\\\\n  1388\\\\t  (vec (sort-by pr-str\\\\n  1389\\\\t                (map (fn [[root path]]\\\\n  1390\\\\t                       [(get occurrence-origins path admission-origin)\\\\n  1391\\\\t                        root path :yang/call-site 1])\\\\n  1392\\\\t                     (vm/application-occurrences row-set)))))\\\\n  1393\\\\t\\\\n  1394\\\\t\\\\n  1395\\\\t(defn expand-batch\\\\n  1396\\\\t  \\\\\\\"Expand one input batch against `ctx` (§3.2). Returns\\\\n  1397\\\\t   `{:status :ok :tree packet :log