\\n  1390\\t                       [(get occurrence-origins path admission-origin)\\n  1391\\t                        root path :yang/call-site 1])\\n  1392\\t                     (vm/application-occurrences row-set)))))\\n  1393\\t\\n  1394\\t\\n  1395\\t(defn expand-batch\\n  1396\\t  \\\"Expand one input batch against `ctx` (§3.2). Returns\\n  1397\\t   `{:status :ok :tree packet :log log :ctx ctx'}` or\\n  1398\\t   `{:status :error :error e :log log :ctx ctx'}`. Either way `ctx'` has\\n  1399\\t   consumed the batch (`:t` + 1) and every attempt it allocated; only\\n  1400\\t   success changes the store, to the post-harvest store. A success also\\n  1401\\t   carries `:frontend-metadata` — the C1 side table finalized over the\\n  1402\\t   final tree (`final-call-site-metadata`), covering the tree that\\n  1403\\t   actually executes — when, and only when, the selected member itself\\n  1404\\t   claimed C1 coverage (its own verdict in `batch-call-site-claims`); a\\n  1405\\t   sibling's claim never manufactures a table for it, and an unclaimed\\n  1406\\t   batch carries no table at all, never an empty one. The admission\\n  1407\\t   this expansion produced the tree under rides beside it as\\n  1408\\t   `:call-site-origin` — the source origin of the admitted run member,\\n  1409\\t   the key the table is stored and resolved under beside the final\\n  1410\\t   root address. It is the table's admission key, not a blanket\\n  1411\\t   stamp: each row's origin is that occurrence's own (§2.1, §2.3) —\\n  1412\\t   a retained occurrence keeps its own incoming provenance (its\\n  1413\\t   source origin, or the generating expansion's, however deeply it\\n  1414\\t   was passed through), and generated syntax carries the\\n  1415\\t   `[:expansion record-address]` of the recorded expansion event\\n  1416\\t   whose output introduced it. A context\\n  1417\\t   store binding a\\n  1418\\t   reserved name, or holding an entry without the current AST contract,\\n  1419\\t   is refused (Rule R): it is a composition defect, so it throws rather\\n  1420\\t   than returning an error.\\\"\\n  1421\\t  [batch ctx]\\n  1422\\t  (check-store! (:store ctx))\\n  1423\\t  (let [ctx (with-default-guards ctx)\\n  1424\\t        source-batch (:t ctx)\\n  1425\\t        base {:ctx ctx, :source-batch source-batch, :events [], :produced []}\\n  1426\\t        finish (fn [st]\\n  1427\\t                 (let [ctx' (update (:ctx st) :t inc)]\\n  1428\\t                   (if-let [e (:error st)]\\n  1429\\t                     {:status :error, :error e, :log (log-packet st), :ctx ctx'}\\n  1430\\t                     {:status :ok, :tree (:tree st), :log (log-packet st),\\n  1431\\t                      :frontend-metadata (:frontend-metadata st),\\n  1432\\t                      :call-site-origin (:call-site-origin st),\\n  1433\\t                      :ctx (assoc ctx' :store (:next-store st))})))\\n  1434\\t        {:keys [admitted error]} (admit batch)]\\n  1435\\t    (if error\\n  1436\\t      (let [[st counter] (allocate-attempt base)]\\n  1437\\t        (finish (-> st\\n  1438\\t                    (record-event (event-row (attempt-id ctx counter) source-batch\\n  1439\\t                                             (source-origin ctx source-batch nil)\\n  1440\\t                                             nil nil nil nil nil error nil))\\n  1441\\t                    (fail error))))\\n  1442\\t      (let [{:keys [trees indexes index run-index definitions]} admitted\\n  1443\\t            store0 (or (:store ctx) {})\\n  1444\\t            store (harvest store0 #(nth indexes %) definitions)\\n  1445\\t            catalogue (into []\\n  1446\\t                            (comp (filter :declared?)\\n  1447\\t                                  (map (fn [{:keys [name tree path value]}]\\n  1448\\t                                         {:name name,\\n  1449\\t                                          :macro-tree (packet-of (nth indexes tree) value),\